    "narrative": "Our lineup enters today with significant momentum, anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.64), who remains the premier play on the board. Facing Tanner Gordon, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a high-park-factor boost and a favorable delivery cadence from the opposing starter that significantly elevates his stolen base potential, a critical metric for our roster composition. **Lawrence Butler** (70.57) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.51) represent our most efficient outfield secondary options; both carry substantial platoon edges against their respective matchups, with **Dylan Beavers** in particular gaining a massive +16% park adjustment that pushes his ceiling well into the \"Strong\" category. Similarly, **JJ Bleday** (68.51) is a mandatory start tonight; his elite +16% SP skill score adjustment and a high-leverage platoon advantage against the struggling Eduardo Rodriguez make him an undervalued contributor in today\u2019s landscape.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation today involved **Luis Arraez** (55.71), who narrowly missed the cut for the starting nine. While **Luis Arraez** offers a high floor for batting average, the optimizer prioritized the higher power-speed upside of **Zack Gelof** (56.00) and **Jonathan Aranda** (58.18) to ensure we maximize our production in counting stats like R and RBI. **Jonathan Aranda** was particularly boosted by a +16% park environment today, which ultimately rendered him the superior tactical choice. We are monitoring **Braden Montgomery** (42.66) on the bench as well, though he remains a \"Below Floor\" play today, specifically due to a 37% rain risk in his matchup against Sean Manaea that introduces too much volatility to override his current projection. All managers should note that since these lineups are currently pending official confirmation, scores are subject to minor adjustments if **Yainer Diaz**, **Cal Raleigh**, or **Brendan Donovan** shift significantly in the batting order.",
